<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018925> rdfs:label "familial or sporadic hemiplegic migraine" ;
    dcterms:description "Hemiplegic migraine (HM) is a rare variety of migraine with aura characterized by the presence of a motor weakness during the aura. Hemiplegic migraine has two main forms depending on the familial history: patients with at least one first- or second-degree relative who has aura including motor weakness have familial hemiplegic migraine (FHM); patients without such familial history have sporadic hemiplegic migraine (SHM)."@en ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Hemiplegic Migraine",
